sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/aristotle-ha06-13> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "In male birds the testicles are visibly larger at pairing time than at other times, most conspicuously in the more salacious birds such as the cock and the cock partridge.";
    dc:type "empirical-generalization";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Bird testes enlarge in the breeding season, most in salacious birds";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Aristotle, The History of Animals (Historia Animalium), Book VI, Part 9; translated by D'Arcy Wentworth Thompson, The Works of Aristotle Translated into English, ed. J. A. Smith and W. D. Ross, Oxford: Clarendon Press, vol. IV (1910). Scope: male birds"
}
